\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Single-factor evaluation of the Maxwell--Kronecker projection over the full campaign range. Panels as in the main paper's single-factor compression test. In~(c) the retained energy fraction approaches the white-noise floor $r/I=1/16$ at $-20$~dB while the \emph  {uncompressed} subspace-leakage ratio $\sigma _{K+1}/\sigma _K$ reaches $0.99$ and the compressed one $0.81$; smaller is better, so this is the diagnostic form of delay-pole collapse, and the separation between the two curves is the margin the projection buys.}}{11}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:s_compression}{{8}{11}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Receiver-mode study over the full campaign range under nested component masks at a common absolute noise level. Panels extend Fig.~\ref {main-fig:c1_combined}(a)--(b) of the main paper. The efficiency ratios of the masked modes below $-10$~dB are conditioned on a small inlier subset and are reported for completeness only.}}{11}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:s_receiver}{{9}{11}{}{}{}}
